WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:01.460
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.124
- [Narrator] It is the
ultimate eternal tribute

00:00:03.124 --> 00:00:05.675
to your first love, your mom.

00:00:05.675 --> 00:00:09.675
The I love mom heart
tattoo, iconic and beloved.

00:00:12.337 --> 00:00:13.839
The history of the mom-centric tribute

00:00:13.839 --> 00:00:15.449
dates back to the 1700s,

00:00:15.449 --> 00:00:18.636
when sailors were at the
forefront of tattoo culture.

00:00:18.636 --> 00:00:21.628
Picture this: you're staring
down a long stint at sea,

00:00:21.628 --> 00:00:23.887
possibly to never return home.

00:00:23.887 --> 00:00:25.967
These said sailors often wanted to keep

00:00:25.967 --> 00:00:27.244
their loved ones close,

00:00:27.244 --> 00:00:29.939
and what could be any loser
than a heart on your arm?

00:00:29.939 --> 00:00:32.301
This heart could symbolize
the heart of a girlfriend,

00:00:32.301 --> 00:00:34.015
a wife, or mom.

00:00:34.015 --> 00:00:36.645
It is even said that mom can
symbolize a love of country,

00:00:36.645 --> 00:00:38.653
the motherland, if you will.

00:00:38.653 --> 00:00:40.855
But nothing says I love mom like this guy,

00:00:40.855 --> 00:00:44.331
Norman Collins, AKA Sailor Jerry.

00:00:44.331 --> 00:00:46.795
Sailor Jerry is the man who popularized

00:00:46.795 --> 00:00:50.627
and polarized the I love mom
tattoo, amongst many others.

00:00:50.627 --> 00:00:52.969
Nowadays, I love mom tattoos
are as popular as ever

00:00:52.969 --> 00:00:56.418
amongst those in the
service and civilians.

00:00:56.418 --> 00:00:58.135
Though the imagery has changed a bit,

00:00:58.135 --> 00:01:00.619
the heartfelt sentiment remains the same.

00:01:00.619 --> 00:01:01.952
We love you mom.

